Body:
> I believe Claude Code switches between Haiku/Opus automatically for efficiency. In OpenCode I can't see any way to use the automatic mode, if it's using Opus 4.5 for everything that would explain why it burns usage so quickly.

@Cyb3rDudu @ilbarone87 @cedws
You need to set in the `opencode.json` file:
```
  “small_model”: “anthropic/claude-haiku-4-5”,

  "agent": {
    "general": {
      "model": "anthropic/claude-haiku-4-5"
    },
    "explore": {
      "model": "anthropic/claude-haiku-4-5"
    },
  }
```

---

You can set any model, or even a different provider, as OpenRouter:
```
  "small_model": "openrouter/x-ai/grok-4.1-fast",

  "agent": {
    "general": {
      "model": "openrouter/x-ai/grok-4.1-fast"
    },
    "explore": {
      "model": "openrouter/x-ai/grok-4.1-fast"
    },
  }
```
